  Here are some tips for the movement key configuration.

  'j' goes down because it descends below the line.
  'k' goes up because it extends upward.
  'h' goes to the left because it's to the left.
  'l' goes to the right because it's to the right.

  The others make a kind of sense in their placement like 'h' and 'l'.

  The main thing is to force yourself to use them exclusively.  Slow
down and work at it as much as necessary.  The more work you put in
early the easier it will be over all.  You'll be amazed how quickly you
pick them up.  You'll also love how much easier NetHack is in general
with your fingers always over the home keys.  


